# Build-context exclusions for the contexts rooted at THIS folder:
#   Dockerfile.cli    (docker-compose `gitnexus`, docker-compose.test `gitnexus-server-test`,
#                      gitops/jobs/image-ci kaniko-cli)
#   Dockerfile.graphs (docker-compose `gitnexus-graphs`)
#
# NOT the web image: Dockerfile.web's context is ./upstream, and Docker reads
# <context>/.dockerignore — upstream/ has its own. This file cannot affect it.
#
# Added 2026-08-20 with the multi-stage Dockerfile.cli. The CLI builder now
# copies from upstream/gitnexus{,-shared}/. On a dev machine those directories
# carry a host-built node_modules/ and a full-history .git/ (~60 MB) that have
# no business in a Linux build context. Dockerfile.cli's COPYs are narrow
# enough that nothing could leak into the image anyway — this is about context
# size and transfer time, and about never tempting a future `COPY upstream/…`
# into shipping a Windows-built native module.
#
# Nothing Dockerfile.cli or Dockerfile.graphs copies is matched below:
#   upstream/gitnexus{,-shared}/{package.json,package-lock.json,tsconfig.json,src,scripts}
#   scripts/*.mjs, scripts/gate-cli-patch-markers.sh, wiki-worker.mjs
#   graphs-sidecar/** (its node_modules is (re)installed inside the image)

**/.git
**/node_modules
**/*.rej
**/*.orig

# Compiled outputs: the builder produces its own; a stale host build must never
# reach a layer.
upstream/gitnexus/dist
upstream/gitnexus-shared/dist
upstream/gitnexus-web/dist
